{"role":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_use","name":"StrReplace","input":{"path":"c:\\Tekcroft\\lib\\franchise-seo-body.html","old_string":"    <div class=\"sec-head mid rv\">\n      <span class=\"smark\"><b>Common questions</b></span>\n      <h2>The questions founders ask <em>before hiring an app developer.</em></h2>\n      <p class=\"sec-lede\">Straight answers on scope, cost, platforms and what happens after launch &mdash;\n        before you commit to anything.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"faq-wrap\" data-at=\"1\">\n\n      <aside class=\"faq-aside rv\" style=\"--d:40ms\">\n        <!-- One layer per question, each holding its own picture, all of\n             them stacked and only one lit. A background-image cannot be\n             transitioned, so swapping the src on a single layer would cut\n             rather than fade; eight layers crossfade with opacity, which\n             can. The pictures are the ones the page already carries â€” no\n             new bytes for this. -->\n        <span class=\"faq-pics\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--faq-shot)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-1)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-2)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-3)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-4)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--cta-shot)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--cn-shot)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--faq-shot)\"></span>\n        </span>\n        <span class=\"faq-aside-eyebrow\">Not on the list?</span>\n        <h3>Ask us the one you came with.</h3>\n        <p>Tell us where your app idea stands today &mdash; what it needs to do, who it is for, and what you have already built. We&rsquo;ll answer straight.</p>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" data-jump>Ask a question</button>\n      </aside>\n\n      <div class=\"faq-list rv\" style=\"--d:80ms\">\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q1\" aria-controls=\"faq-a1\" aria-expanded=\"true\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">01</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Do I need a full development company, or should I validate my idea first?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q1\" data-open=\"true\">\n            <div><p>If you&rsquo;re pre-revenue, validate your idea before investing in a full build. Use a landing page, prototype, or small validation build to test demand quickly and affordably. Once you have real users, paying customers, and clear requirements, it&rsquo;s time to consider a full development team.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q2\" aria-controls=\"faq-a2\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">02</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">How does your pricing structure work?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q2\">\n            <div><p>Milestone-based, and in writing before work starts. The scope is agreed screen by screen, then you pay per milestone: on prototype sign-off, for each build sprint as it ships, and at launch &mdash; not as a large deposit against a date six months out. Typical ranges run $10,000&ndash;$30,000 for a simple MVP, $30,000&ndash;$80,000 for a mid-complexity app, and $80,000&ndash;$400,000+ for enterprise-grade work.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q3\" aria-controls=\"faq-a3\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">03</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">What should I prepare before reaching out for a quote?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q3\">\n            <div><p>The single most useful thing you can bring us is a screen-by-screen breakdown of what your app needs to do, written as if you had to explain it to someone with zero context. It needs to be specific, because it makes the quote you get comparable.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q4\" aria-controls=\"faq-a4\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">04</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Native or cross-platform, which one should I choose?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q4\">\n            <div><p>We wouldn&rsquo;t recommend building two native apps just because you eventually want to be on both stores. If you&rsquo;re still proving the product, the extra development cost may be better spent getting the first version in front of users. The exceptions are performance-heavy products and apps relying heavily on native device capabilities.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q5\" aria-controls=\"faq-a5\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">05</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Can you build for both iOS and Android at once?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q5\">\n            <div><p>Yes. We can take either route: two native applications or one shared Flutter or React Native codebase. The decision comes down to the product and performance requirements, as well as how quickly you need both versions live.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q6\" aria-controls=\"faq-a6\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">06</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Can you build an MVP first before a full build?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a6\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q6\">\n            <div><p>An MVP is often the better starting point. It puts the core product in users&rsquo; hands sooner and gives you evidence about what people actually use before you spend on the full feature set.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q7\" aria-controls=\"faq-a7\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">07</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">What does year two look like? What happens after launch?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a7\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q7\">\n            <div><p>The same team stays on. That means crash and performance monitoring from launch week, OS updates and security patches every month, and feature work when you&rsquo;re ready for version two. Budget for it: annual maintenance typically runs 15&ndash;20% of the original build cost.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q8\" aria-controls=\"faq-a8\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">08</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">What should I actually look for when hiring a mobile app development company?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a8\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q8\">\n            <div><p>Start with technical fit. Can the company fit your product&rsquo;s requirements? Then look at relevant experience and how clearly they handle scope and pricing. One more question to ask before you sign: who owns the app after it goes live?</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>","new_string":"    <div class=\"sec-head mid rv\">\n      <span class=\"smark\"><b>Common questions</b></span>\n      <h2>The questions franchise brands ask <em>before hiring a franchise SEO agency.</em></h2>\n      <p class=\"sec-lede\">Straight answers on cost, scale, AI visibility and timelines &mdash;\n        before you commit to anything.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"faq-wrap\" data-at=\"1\">\n\n      <aside class=\"faq-aside rv\" style=\"--d:40ms\">\n        <!-- One layer per question, each holding its own picture, all of\n             them stacked and only one lit. A background-image cannot be\n             transitioned, so swapping the src on a single layer would cut\n             rather than fade; layers crossfade with opacity, which can.\n             The pictures are the ones the page already carries â€” no\n             new bytes for this. -->\n        <span class=\"faq-pics\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--faq-shot)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-1)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-2)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-3)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--shot-4)\"></span>\n          <span class=\"faq-pic\" style=\"--pic:var(--cta-shot)\"></span>\n        </span>\n        <span class=\"faq-aside-eyebrow\">Not on the list?</span>\n        <h3>Ask us the one you came with.</h3>\n        <p>Tell us where your franchise network stands today &mdash; how many locations, which markets, and what you have already tried. We&rsquo;ll answer straight.</p>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" type=\"button\" data-jump>Ask a question</button>\n      </aside>\n\n      <div class=\"faq-list rv\" style=\"--d:80ms\">\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q1\" aria-controls=\"faq-a1\" aria-expanded=\"true\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">01</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">What is the difference between franchise SEO and local SEO?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q1\" data-open=\"true\">\n            <div><p>Local SEO focuses on a single business, while Franchise SEO requires focusing on all locations of a brand. Additionally, there are other considerations, like making sure all locations use the same brand elements and avoiding duplicate content.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q2\" aria-controls=\"faq-a2\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">02</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">How much does franchise SEO cost?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q2\">\n            <div><p>The price of franchise SEO has several factors, including the overall size of the franchise, how competitive the market is, the amount of technical and content requirements for each location, and many other considerations. In general, smaller franchises can expect to pay a few thousand dollars a month, whereas larger franchises may pay in the tens of thousands of dollars a month.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q3\" aria-controls=\"faq-a3\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">03</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Can Tekcroft manage SEO for hundreds of locations?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q3\">\n            <div><p>Tekcroft&rsquo;s process is built to scale, from keyword mapping and GBP management to technical SEO and reporting. Doesn&rsquo;t matter if you operate 10 locations or several hundred.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q4\" aria-controls=\"faq-a4\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">04</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">Do you help with AI search visibility, not just Google rankings?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q4\">\n            <div><p>Yes. AI Overviews and AI-generated answers now appear across the majority of franchise-related searches. We build content and structured data specifically to earn visibility and citation in AI search results, not just traditional rankings.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q5\" aria-controls=\"faq-a5\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">05</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">How do you report results across a franchise network?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q5\">\n            <div><p>You get both a brand-level view and a location-level view in the same reporting cycle; underperforming markets are visible immediately.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"faq-item\">\n          <button class=\"faq-q\" type=\"button\" id=\"faq-q6\" aria-controls=\"faq-a6\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n            <span class=\"faq-n\">06</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-t\">How long does franchise SEO take to show results?</span>\n            <span class=\"faq-sign\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n              <svg class=\"plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M12 5v14M5 12h14\"/></svg>\n              <svg class=\"x\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"><path d=\"M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18\"/></svg>\n            </span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"faq-a\" id=\"faq-a6\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-q6\">\n            <div><p>Technical fixes, listing standardization, and governance setup begin in the first 30&ndash;60 days. Ranking and traffic movement are decided by market competitiveness, but most franchise programs start seeing measurable location-level movement within 3&ndash;6 months.</p></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n    </div>"}}]}}
